						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12722#msg12722"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12722#msg12722">Re: Sibling Punishment. . .?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> November 17, 2004, 05:36:25 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12697#msg12697">Quote from: Moraganna on November 16, 2004, 03:26:04 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12694#msg12694">Quote from: Needaa on November 16, 2004, 12:08:36 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I should come out of my box?&nbsp; Foster parenting has taught me a lot Moraganna and one of the first things I suggest NO COMMAND is that communication be established between the parents and the children!&nbsp; If parents are too busy then maybe a reality check is in order i.e. a phone call to Children &amp; Youth Services would help them wake up.&nbsp; <br /><br />As far as condoning welfare mothers popping out babies, I&#039;m the one that gets to see these kids first hand, especially when their parents are to damned high or drunk and these kids run the streets without the love, care or nurtuing of GOOD parents.&nbsp; SO PLEASE&nbsp; DON&#039;T EVEN GO THERE! These children are the victims and don&#039;t ever think for one minute I would stand up for such parents.&nbsp; Matter of fact, I think the welfare system is backwards...instead of &quot;rewarding&quot; mothers for having more children by paying them more, they should be rewarding the mothers who are consciously making an effort to become independent and STOP having children we ultimately end up paying for!<br /><br />There is nothing I REPEAT nothing wrong with asking your older children to babysit occasionally provided there is a good reason and they are responsible enough to be trusted.<br /><br />What was the church meeting about???? Was it marriage counseling?&nbsp; Geeez, I wouldn&#039;t want my children to know that mom and dad may have problems that they are trying to work out for the good of the family.&nbsp; Why would I want to scare my children when such a devasting situation might never take place?&nbsp; OR what if the older brother has problems that need to be work out through counseling?&nbsp; Either way, it&#039;s none of our business.&nbsp; The only thing that IS our business is trying to help Naithien, not to diss his parents.<br /><br />Agreed Naithien has his problems with his parents but ONLY through communication does this resolve itself.&nbsp; You only see it through a child&#039;s eyes as justifiably you are still quite young.&nbsp; I&#039;ve seen it both ways and let me tell you, you probably won&#039;t understand it all until you&#039;ve walked a few miles in my shoes.<br /><br />See how you feel 20+ years from now, when you have a family.&nbsp; Until then, please don&#039;t go twisting my words and assuming that you have all the answers.&nbsp; Parenting is not as easy as it looks.<br /></div><br />Maybe if parents would take care of their children you would not be a foster parent!!! Just goes to show that not every family is picture perfect.<br /><br />I never said the children are not victims, thus my whole damn point you idiot! Parents have to be responcible for their actions and take care of the kids they create NOT the fuckin kids they made to begin with!!! It is not a childs responcibility to take care of their siblings I don&#039;t give a shit how you cut it ... that is a parents JOB!!<br /><br />Although I TOTALLY agree with the welfare system and the fact it should be totally removed. Fathers want to be dead beat dads, take their pay checks for force them to work. Mothers who want to use abuse drugs or alcohol and get pregnant have no buisness having kids in the first place!<br /><br />There is everything wrong with asking an older sibling to watch a younger one. My ex husband was in the military and on the military posts they have firm laws preventing any child under the age of 18 from being left home alone PERIOD without an adult watching them. GET IT?? These are children and as children they should be treated as such and have an ADULT to watch them.<br /><br />If it was marriage counciling I highly doubt the oldest sibling would have gone with the mother. Also may I enlighten you, children normally know when there is a problem in the family before both parents do, if both parents do not already know. <br /><br />He made it our buisness when he brought it to these boards. If Nait had felt comfortable talking to his parents about this issue do you really think he would have brought it here for us the public to read? I highly doubt that!<br /><br />I strongly hope you are not calling me a child, you do not know my life or what I have been through. But you are being very narrow minded. As for you bring a foster parent, as I am sure there are a few very good ones, most of the ones out there are just as corrupt if not worse then the parents of the children they were taken from.<br /><br /><br /></div><br />I agree with much of what Moraganna said, and luckily for me; I don&#039;t have a problem with nasty posts, but I&#039;ll try to resist this time.<br /><br />I feel mainly the way Moraganna described, when I was younger my mom always hired a 20+ sitter who was really nice to us and treated us with respect- even when it came to punishing- but now that she has my older sibling and I, she feels that we&#039;re responsible enough and that we&#039;re comfortable enough. <br />&nbsp; &nbsp;But when handling 3 younger siblings who have no respect for me or patience or even sense of responsibility, especially without motivation, its not as easy as it looks. And thus I am forced to use more drastic measures without being physical.<br /><br />When ordered to go to their room, they refuse with the common &quot;You&#039;re not the boss of me&quot; So I am forced to take away certain privlages. (Gamecube Controllers, Computer power cords, etc.) <br /><br />Am I responsible enough to be trusted IRL? I think so. But what Needaa was saying is, imo, bullshit
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
