						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12728#msg12728"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12728#msg12728">Re: Sibling Punishment. . .?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #20 on:</b> November 18, 2004, 02:06:49 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think you do fine w/ your punishment.&nbsp; But how old are they again?&nbsp; Please, if they are young like just an example but 1-6.. do not expect respect out of them.&nbsp; They are children and do not understand respect.&nbsp; They have always looked at you as their brother who plays with them not their babysitter who bosses them.&nbsp; &nbsp;I see both Moraganna and Needaa&#039;s points.&nbsp; I am not gonna get into it because no matter what people are not gonna all raise their children the same, and because you do things a way in your home does not mean everyone else should be the same way.&nbsp; I would definitely NEVER absolutely NEVER leave all of my kids alone home together, I would have no home by the time I got back.&nbsp; They are my kids, I love them, I stay home with them and they are worse than the simpson kids.&nbsp; I have left my older daughter with my youngest but that was for 15 min.&nbsp; That was fine.&nbsp; <br />Anyways Nathein, tell your parents how you feel, I do believe if they trust you enough to babysit, then they will listen to how you feel.&nbsp; Good Luck /hug
