	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12730"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=345" title="View the profile of Dwalion SoulVoid">Dwalion SoulVoid</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 95<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								Gnomercy~!!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=345"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12730#msg12730"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1273.msg12730#msg12730">Re: Sibling Punishment. . .?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #21 on:</b> November 18, 2004, 04:06:41 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Hey I want to chime in!<br /><br /><br />/cackle<br /><br />To my knowledge and experience, UCMJ does not cover unattended minors.&nbsp; Military Law dictates that when Military Law does not cover a specific topic, it will fall under Federal and/or State Law (I don&#039;t know about out of the country, ask someone who has been stationed outside the US).<br /><br />True story, while I was on patrol, stationed in Maine, got a call from a concerned neighbor about a sailor leaving her 8 year old daughter home alone.&nbsp; Me being the concerned parent that I am and a concerned person, plus knowing who the sailor was, someone I considered a friend and was one of my subordinates, went directly to the residence and coax the 8 year old to let me and my partner in.&nbsp; I asked the 8 year old where her mother went and she did not even know she was gone.&nbsp; The sailor/mother in question was your typical partier and we knew she would be at the base club, so I went directly there, leaving my partner with the 8 year old and got her out the club and asked her what she was doing leaving her daughter home alone.&nbsp; She agreed it wasn&#039;t a brilliant idea and we came directly back.&nbsp; I filled out an incident report, called my chief, he came to the office and began searching the law books to see if we have to book her for anything.&nbsp; We had some other things that came up, had to go, made our way back to the office and we read through all of our law books to no avail.&nbsp; Finally the chief stumbled onto it in the Maine State law book.&nbsp; Stated something to the effect that there is no age law, only IF and WHEN something (jeopardizes the safety/welfare) happens to the minor.&nbsp; &nbsp;...wtf...&nbsp; Needless to say, you will hear horror stories of some places, this was in Maine..&nbsp; I am sure its gotta be different in more forward thinking states.&nbsp; At that time, nothing was/could be done, but person to person I told her if she needs a baby sitter for when she wants to go out, my (x)wife could do it for free and not to do that shit anymore.&nbsp; In the event we showed up and she was hurt (obviously) or there was a pot boiling on the stove (clearly) or there were a rash of rapes/break-ins (almost gray) to filth/stench backed up toilet etc (gray), then she would of fallen under child abuse, which we didnt consider since it was relatively safe situation once we arrived on scene.<br /><br />Here are some links.<br /><br /><a href="http://www.au.af.mil/au/awc/awcgate/ucmj.htm" target="_blank">http://www.au.af.mil/au/awc/awcgate/ucmj.htm</a><br /><br /><a href="http://www.au.af.mil/au/awc/awcgate/awc-law.htm#ucmj" target="_blank">http://www.au.af.mil/au/awc/awcgate/awc-law.htm#ucmj</a><br /><br />Here is a Q&amp;A from an Airforce website from somewhere in Utah.&nbsp; Read the part about kids alone in a running car in the heat.<br /><br /><a href="http://www.hilltoptimes.com/ActionLine.asp?edition=66" target="_blank">http://www.hilltoptimes.com/ActionLine.asp?edition=66</a><br /><br />Now, not trying to derail your thread kiddo, so I&#039;ll give you some advice.<br /><br />You need confidence, like others said, speak with your parents about how you feel, sounds like you guys might be religious, so I am sure you can speak with your clergy about this as well.&nbsp; Treating your siblings as you would want to be treated, with respect, love and concern, you can never go wrong, and if you do, know that you are trying.&nbsp; To counter siblings questioning your authority as their older brother, take a step back and evaluate how you act when parents are there and how they are when they are not, always be who you are, their older brother, then the understand and respect will grow.&nbsp; Like Kilaer said, you cannot expect someone who doesn&#039;t know any better to act like they do, even as a parent who has direct control and authority over their children, they are what they call &#039;growing pains&#039; testing someone&#039;s limits, I myself am going through the No stage where my daughter only says NO.&nbsp; Just know they are your loved ones and treat them with it.&nbsp; Give them big hugs and kiss them, tickle them, say their feet stink and give them nice snacks.&nbsp; Nothing wrong with that.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Dwalion SoulVoid &lt;Arirang&gt;<br />70 Necromancer <br /><br />You will more than likely post something stupid and I will respond with something witty.&nbsp; I will more than likely post something stupid and you will respond with something witty.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12731"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=15" title="View the profile of Killy">Killy</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Goddess of Whips and Rezzes<br />
								Moderator<br />
